#This is used to display the NPC's dialogues.
Priest: {
	DayChat1: It feels like everyone's committing sins left and right these days.
	DayChat2: I'm no pillar of judgement, but the lord certainly is. And he thinks these townsfolk could be doing much better!
	DayChat3: Peace be with you, {0}. Have you come to seek my counsel?
	DayChat4: The lord could offer you great blessings if you simply learned how to embrace them. For a hero like yourself, that comes in handy!
	DayChat5: Ah, sorry, I was just reading one of my scriptures. How may I assist you?
	NightChat1: Service today was very pleasant. Only a few people arrived, but at least they stayed for the food!
	NightChat2: I'm not worried about nightmares. I have the lord watch over me while I sleep.
	NightChat3: A good night's sleep is always important. I wake up extra early, just to pray!
	HomelessChat1: I best be taking my leave now. I have a trek of self-realization I must follow!
	HomelessChat2: It has been a while since I've been in a town. Do people still read illuminated manuscripts?
	HomelessChat3:
		'''
		The outside life is not the life for me, I'm afraid. I would
		much prefer a church, or mosque... or perhaps a synagogue!
		'''
	WindyChat1: These gales are ringing my steeple's beautiful bells! O, what a symphony!
	WindyChat2: I saw something flying away earlier, and now I think it was my other robe...
	RainChat1: When it rains, they say it is the lord's tears.
	RainChat2: Dear lord, please make this rain go away. Amen.
	StormChat1: "'TIS THE GREAT FLOODING!! WHY... WHY ISN'T ANYONE FEARING THE WRATH OF GOD?!"
	StormChat2: The ark is almost ready, but no one's getting on! Has every person here lost their mind?!
	PartyChat1: Splendid, this party is just like mass! Remember to save your cupcakes until after prayers, everyone!
	PartyChat2: Well, maybe I can let a little loose just this once–no, no, I mustn't.
	GraveyardChat1: Best be careful around these grounds. Even the slightest disruption could anger the spirits who rest here...
	GraveyardChat2: ...and so we pray for the fallen, may they seek peace as they walk into their eternal slumber...
	BloodMoonChat1: Hark! What sinister creatures the night has brought... May you strike them down with your fervorish hand!
	BloodMoonChat2: Are these red skies a divine act of punishment!? Lord have mercy...
	BloodMoonChat3: Here, take this dagger. Clearly the lord hasn't gotten a good sacrifice in a while.
	MartianChat1: I don't suppose those space folk would be interested in adopting our religion?
	MartianChat2: Those martians came from the heavens, but they certainly aren't angels. I'm not sure what to make of this.
	PainterChat: That {0} gentleman is just who I need for my mural!
	TaxCollectorChat: '''{0} called my religion a "ploy just to steal money", the nerve!'''
	CyborgChat: Yes, I believe even a machine like {0} is capable of sin.
}
